From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ethan Hill <ethan.hill1999@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:52:13 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] CandyOS P38: preference row switch is the 4.4 framework
 Holo switch

preference_widget_switch_compat - the widget layout androidx
SwitchPreferenceCompat inflates for every row toggle - drops the
M3 MaterialSwitch (and its Theme.Material3.DynamicColors.DayNight
overlay, which force-styled rows Material even on the Holo
cascade) for the plain android.widget.Switch. It renders the
SettingsLib switchStyle (now the 4.4 Holo switch, CandyOS P38 in
frameworks/base) via the theme's android:switchStyle; androidx
SwitchPreferenceCompat binds any Checkable (the non-SwitchCompat
branch of syncSwitchView), so state sync is unchanged.

Change-Id: I807cfa04b2651727896de288aa4c737b8c9457e9
---
 res/layout/preference_widget_switch_compat.xml | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/res/layout/preference_widget_switch_compat.xml b/res/layout/preference_widget_switch_compat.xml
index e833171d5da..b57f811b928 100644
--- a/res/layout/preference_widget_switch_compat.xml
+++ b/res/layout/preference_widget_switch_compat.xml
@@ -15,12 +15,17 @@
   ~ limitations under the License.
   -->
 
-<com.google.android.material.materialswitch.MaterialSwitch
+<!-- KitKat UI Project (P38): the row toggle is the 4.4 framework Holo
+     switch (android.widget.Switch), replacing the M3 MaterialSwitch with
+     its DayNight overlay. androidx SwitchPreferenceCompat binds any
+     Checkable, and the Holo track/thumb drawables come from the theme's
+     android:switchStyle (Switch.SettingsLib, parented to
+     Widget.Holo.CompoundButton.Switch by the SettingsLib P38 change). -->
+<Switch
     xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
     android:id="@+id/switchWidget"
     android:layout_width="wrap_content"
     android:layout_height="wrap_content"
     android:background="@null"
     android:clickable="false"
-    android:focusable="false"
-    android:theme="@style/Theme.Material3.DynamicColors.DayNight" />
+    android:focusable="false" />
